("Which phrase is redundant?","absolutely essential|very essential|essential|most essential",0,"Essential is absolute by definition.","Conciseness"),
("Which sentence is most concise?","Due to the fact that it rained, we stayed home.|Because it rained, we stayed home.|Owing to the rain, we remained at home.|In view of the rain, we chose to stay home.",1,"'Because' is shortest and clearest.","Conciseness"),
("'Fewer' is correctly used with","countable nouns|uncountable nouns|abstract nouns only|singular nouns",0,"Fewer books, less water.","Diction"),
("Choose correctly: 'The new policy will ___ every department.'","affect|effect|effectuate|affection",0,"Verb 'affect' = influence.","Diction"),
("Choose correctly: 'The ___ of the experiment was surprising.'","affect|effect|affective|affected",1,"Noun 'effect' = result.","Diction"),
("Choose: 'She ___ the book on the table.'","lay|laid|lain|lie",1,"Past tense of transitive 'lay' is 'laid'.","Diction"),
("Choose: 'He ___ down for an hour.'","lay|laid|lied|lain",0,"Past of intransitive 'lie' is 'lay'.","Diction"),
("The head of a school is its","principal|principle|principals|principality",0,"'Principal' = the head.","Diction"),
("A firm's ___ are its standards.","principles|principals|principal|principle",0,"'Principles' = moral rules.","Diction"),
("A word completing praise is a","complement|compliment|compilation|complementation",1,"A 'compliment' is praise.","Diction"),
("Parked cars must be ___; writing paper is ___.","stationary / stationery|stationery / stationary|stationary / stationary|stationery / stationery",0,"Stationary = still; stationery = paper.","Diction"),
("An indirect reference to a work is an","allusion|illusion|elusion|delusion",0,"An 'allusion' references another work.","Diction"),
("A ___ employee is one expected to join soon.","perspective|prospective|prospers|prospectus",1,"'Prospective' = future/expected.","Diction"),
("A judge must be ___ (impartial).","disinterested|uninterested|interested|dis-interesting",0,"'Disinterested' = impartial.","Diction"),
("'Not only did she win, ___ she broke the record.'","but also|and|but|so",0,"The correlative pair is 'not only... but also'.","Correlatives"),
("'Between you and ___, the plan is risky.'","I|me|myself|mine",1,"Object of preposition: 'me'.","Pronouns"),
("Who' is used for people; ___ is used for things.","whom|which|that|who's",1,"'Which' for things; 'that' also restricts things.","Pronouns"),
("In a list of three, use the ___ degree of an adjective: 'the ___ of the three'.","comparative|superlative|positive|absolute",1,"Among three or more, superlative.","Usage"),
("'The data ___ published monthly.' Choose the convention used in scientific writing.","is|are|was|has been",1,"In formal statistics usage, plural 'are' is common for data.","Agreement"),
("'If she ___ studied, she would have passed.'","had|has|would have|did",0,"Past perfect in the unreal conditional.","Verb tense"),
("'___ the rain, the match continued.' Choose the best preposition.","Despite of|Despite|Although|In spite",1,"'Despite' takes no 'of'.","Usage"),
("Which idiom is correct?","comply to|comply with|comply for|comply at",1,"'Comply with' is the standard collocation.","Usage"),
("Which is correct?","capable to do|capable of doing|capable in doing|capable for doing",1,"'Capable of' + gerund.","Usage"),
